Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0004.
DeepSeek-V4.1: hand the model's quant config to its lm_head (ParallelLMHead), so a quantization plugin can quantize the
head. A no-op for the checkpoint's own FP8 config: Fp8Config.get_quant_method returns no method for embeddings and the
head stays UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod. The recipe's vllm_exl3_moe plugin uses it for an opt-in MXFP8 head through Marlin:
the BF16 head reads 0.66 GB per forward per rank at TP=2, and the DSpark drafter shares the module, so a decode step pays
it twice.

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py
index bd91e8f..bec0353 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py
@@ -1525,9 +1525,12 @@ class DeepseekV41LLMForCausalLM(
             vllm_config=vllm_config, prefix=maybe_prefix(prefix, "model")
         )
         if get_pp_group().is_last_rank:
+            # The quant config may quantize the head (a no-op for the checkpoint's own FP8 config, which
+            # hands embeddings no method). The DSpark drafter shares this module, so it reads the same head.
             self.lm_head = ParallelLMHead(
                 config.vocab_size,
                 config.hidden_size,
+                quant_config=vllm_config.quant_config,
                 prefix=maybe_prefix(prefix, "lm_head"),
             )
         else:
